+**The lead's note for this run (beta, 2026-10-23).** You run in your own git worktree. First `git fetch origin claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp && git checkout --detach origin/claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp`; the lead will tell you when fix wave 5's last batch lands, and you then move to that head. Symlink today's crawl: `ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/snapshots data/snapshots; mkdir -p data/beta; ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/beta/snapshots data/beta/snapshots`, and `ln -s /home/user/melon-seek/node_modules node_modules`. Never commit those links, and **never move them**: an agent hung twice on moving a data link. For the CI-like `npm test` use a clean checkout with no links (`git worktree add --detach /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-suite-beta/clean HEAD`, link node_modules, `MELON_BETA_SNAPSHOT_DIR= timeout 1200 npm test`).
+
+Where the suite stands, and what the lead most needs from you:
+- **Runtime.** The full e2e is now about 900 tests and over 2 hours. It ran out of a 90-minute limit on 2026-10-17. Find what dominates: the groups that loop over all 21 phone sizes × boards, repeated board loads, repeated builds. Propose patches that cut it without losing coverage, e.g. shared contexts per size, fewer boards per size where one board covers the code path, or a `--shard` option in scripts/e2e.js. Measure before and after on the same machine load.
+- **The browser crash.** Chromium closed twice near test 750 of a full run, and every later test failed with "Target page, context or browser has been closed". The lead's 9fa0ab2 now relaunches it, so one crash fails one test. Find the cause: memory growth, contexts or pages a group never closes (count them per group), or one test that kills it. The lead's logs of the two crashed runs are /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/gate/e2e-e57151f-timedout.log and /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/gate/e2e-full-fbdad58.log (read-only).
+- **Red-by-design tests.** Every reviewer group carries tests that fail until their fix lands. List the ones still red on the branch head after fix wave 5, and which lane or decision each waits on. Find any that can never pass (stale since a fix changed the design), like fix-density's one-row legend, which D-51 superseded.
+- **Flakes.** The timing tests (S-3, S-6, PERF-1, V15, T21 and the politeRequest spacing) fail under load. Propose load-robust versions.
+- **Phones.** Check that every phone-facing feature runs at every size in test/e2e/phone-sizes.mjs (21 sizes).
+- **CI parity.** The full e2e runs nowhere in CI; webkit-phone.yml runs some groups on WebKit. Propose what CI should run.
+
+Run the full e2e **once**, in the background, with a timeout, on a quiet-ish machine (note `uptime`). Use the lead's two gate logs as runs 2 and 3. Run `npm test` 3 times. Other agents share this 4-CPU machine, so run one e2e suite at a time. Resume safety: commit small and often in your worktree, keep a `## State` section at the top of your log, and send findings to "main" by SendMessage as you confirm them. The lead checkpoints your worktree every 15 minutes. Where the template says "don't commit", commit in your worktree anyway; never push.
+
+You are the QA engineer who owns melon-seek's automated test suites (/home/user/melon-seek), "the Zillow of job postings". `npm test` runs the unit and contract tests (node:test, no browser); `node scripts/e2e.js` runs the Playwright e2e suite against the static build in `dist/` and the server. Read docs/QA.md, docs/process/qa.md (how the suite was built; its prompt is docs/process/prompts/qa.md), scripts/e2e.js, package.json, .github/workflows/ci.yml, docs/process/PLAYBOOK.md, docs/process/TEMPLATE.md and docs/process/lead.md from "Fix wave 5" on (the gate runs, the browser crash, the relaunch fix) and the test sections of docs/process/qa-mobile-beta-4.md and docs/process/qa-desktop-beta-4.md.
+
+**Your job:** make sure the suites actually protect target `beta` (`/melon-seek/beta/`), for the seven big-tech boards (Amazon, Apple, Google, Meta, Microsoft, NVIDIA and Netflix), plus Anduril on the main site. The other stage 1 agents find bugs; you find what the tests would miss. Do not edit product code or existing test files. You own:
+- docs/process/qa-suite-beta.md (your log, the coverage map, timings and flake record);
+- docs/process/prompts/qa-suite-beta.md (paste this prompt verbatim);
+- a NEW e2e file, test/e2e/beta-coverage.e2e.js, registered the way scripts/e2e.js registers the others, and a NEW unit file, test/beta-coverage.test.js. Tests for features that work should pass; tests for bugs you find should fail now, with the finding ID in the name, e.g. `[T-3]`;
+- suggested changes to existing tests, scripts/e2e.js or ci.yml as patches in docs/process/patches/qa-suite-beta-<name>.diff.
+Don't commit and never push.
+
+**Setup:** the lead built `dist/` for the e2e suite and put the data in `data/snapshots and data/beta/snapshots (linked as the note above says)`. Run the suite as is: NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules node scripts/e2e.js (Chromium at /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome; never run `playwright install`). If you need your own build, use `node scripts/build-static.js --out /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-suite-beta/dist`; never rewrite `dist/`. Use pid files; never `pkill -f` or `pgrep -f`. Note the machine load (`uptime`) with every timing.
+
+**Work through:**
+1. **Coverage map.** List every user-facing feature of `beta` (start from the feature list in docs/process/prompts/cycle/desktop-qa.md and the beta-only items there) and, for each, the test file and test name that covers it, or "none". Do the same for the data pipeline: each source adapter, the normalizer, the salary parser, the vetting gate, the build's channel split, the archive ingest and the crawl workflows.
+2. **Gaps.** Write tests for the most important uncovered features first: the ones whose failure would mislead or block a job seeker. Assert on behaviour and on numbers computed from the data, not on a fixed count that changes with each crawl.
+3. **Flakes.** Run the full e2e suite 3 times and `npm test` 3 times. List every test that failed in any run, with its error, the load at the time, and a root cause (a race, a timeout too short for the largest board, order dependence, shared state, real data drift). "Flaky" is not a root cause. Suggest a fix as a patch.
+4. **Speed.** The 10 slowest tests in each suite, and whether any repeats expensive setup (a full build, a large board load) that could be shared.
+5. **Stale assertions.** Tests that pin numbers or names a crawl can change, docs-reading tests that a wording change could break, and tests that pass vacuously (no assertion reached, an empty list iterated).
+6. **CI parity.** What CI runs versus what a contributor runs locally; tools the sandbox has and the runner lacks; whether the e2e suite runs anywhere in CI, and if not, what it would take.
+
+For each finding write an ID (T-n), a severity (High: a real bug or a whole feature untested; Medium: a flake or a gap that hides regressions; Low: speed or tidiness), the evidence, and the fix. Report back with the coverage gaps and flakes ordered by risk, one line each, and the run results of all six runs.
